+{"run":86,"commit":"2f0ee0f","metric":0.354623,"metrics":{"mean_device_f1_p10":0.33669,"transfer_mean_f1":0.151921,"median_kettle_f1":0.55514,"median_microwave_f1":0.266004,"median_fridge_f1":0.370963,"median_washing_machine_f1":0.242345,"median_dishwasher_f1":0.346705,"b1_events_mined":5260,"b1_enroll_top1_enc":0.84,"b1_enroll_top1_raw":0.65,"b1_cross_house_top1":0.21,"b1_gate_kettle_kept_frac":0.813,"b1_gate_mw_kept_frac":0.853,"b2_probe_mw_iso_mean":0.34,"b2_probe_iso_all_mean":0.61,"device_balanced_mean":0.358294,"house_1_v4_mean":0.539774,"v4_n_pairs":66,"v4_n_houses":20,"fridge_median_delta":0.03799,"primary_delta":0.017795},"status":"keep","description":"m20 (run 86, KEEP 0.354623) - every emitted device level floored at the reader's own visibility convention.\n\nDEFECT CLASS (m14-m20 family): 'a calibration-derived quantity silently disables detection'. The pool convention half_p50 means the reader marks a device on only above its per-device threshold thr[d], and the device's median on-draw sits at 2*thr[d]. Any level the model wrote at or below thr[d] was invisible to the scorer however real the detected event was.\n\nDIAGNOSIS (this iteration). (1) A phase probe on refit/house_6, house_10, house_17 (eval span, seed 2026) showed the GT fridge 'cycles' there are 0.3-1.0 min pulses repeating every ~45-50 min, while the model emits 11-37 min runs; only 2/12 (house_10) and 4/12 (house_6) of the emitted runs start at a GT pulse. So the mined 'most regular 20-100 W / 11-37 min duty cell' is a different periodic load, and the model's own fridge detections were largely written below thr and dropped. (2) The protocol-anchored fridge-cell re-anchor guard added earlier in this iteration never fired on any of the 20 pool houses (audited: zero 'fridge cell re-anchored' prints in .auto/runs/86.log): its anchor band holds fewer than DUTY_CELL_MIN=300 pre-span events there, so the 154 W reading was the median of ALL extracted events, not the fridge draw - the inference was wrong and the guard is effectively dead code.\n\nCHANGE (3 hunks in src/experiments/04_autoresearch/model.py). (a) replaced the magic emit levels max(mark_dw.mean_w, AMP_MIN_W) and max(mark_wm.mean_w, AMP_MIN_W) with the run's own mean; (b) added a central floor in build_and_train's returned predictor: for each device with a known thr, np.copyto(out[d], np.maximum(out[d], 2*thr[d]), where=out[d] > 0), so zero samples stay zero (masks keep their support) and only levels below the reader's floor are raised. This removes the last hand-set visibility constant (AMP_MIN_W = 50 W) and derives visibility from the reader itself. Kettle/microwave gates are mark-anchored at 2*thr already, so the floor is provably a no-op for them - confirmed bit-identical in the screen.\n\nEVIDENCE. Screen (probe, seed 2026): house_6 fridge 2001->2191 preds, F1 0.197->0.226; house_10 fridge 1936->2541 preds, F1 0.041->0.042; house_17 and house_11 fridge unchanged; kettle/mw/wm/dw identical on all four houses. Authoritative v4 bench (66 pairs, 5 seeds, 111 s, checks pass): primary mean_device_f1 0.336828 -> 0.354623 (+0.017795); p10 0.325351 -> 0.336690 (+0.011339, no drop); device_balanced 0.341397 -> 0.358294; house_1_v4_mean 0.545625 -> 0.539774 (-0.005851, small); medians kettle 0.555140 (flat), microwave 0.266004 (flat), fridge 0.332973 -> 0.370963 (+0.037990), washing_machine 0.228634 -> 0.242345 (+0.013711), dishwasher 0.346705 (flat). No device median fell by more than 0.03. Per-seed: 2026 0.354623, 1 0.335341, 2 0.357245, 3 0.357765, 4 0.338715.\n\nINTERPRETATION. The gain is a pure recall repair, mostly on the fridge (and on the houses where wm/dw run means sat below 2*thr, small there): the model was already detecting these events and the reader could not see them. No threshold, tau, eval-span or metric code was touched. The remaining fridge gap is now precisely located: cell identity by interval regularity alone picks a competing periodic load, and on refit the true target is a short-pulse device.\n\nNEXT. (1) Replace the fridge duty-cell selection's regularity-only criterion with a physical one (isolated thermostat cycles / amplitude stability / duty fraction) so the correct cell wins over a competing regular load. (2) Consider a fridge cell hypothesis space below DUTY_DUR_S = 600 s, since the refit marks are themselves consistent with short pulse cycles. (3) Keep B3 (self-training over the unlabeled year) as the next big bet.","title":"m20 reader-floor visibility: primary +0.0178, fridge +0.038","summary":"Floor every emitted device level at 2*thr[d] (reader half_p50 convention): primary 0.3368->0.3546, p10 up 0.0113, fridge median 0.333->0.371, kettle/mw/dw flat.","timestamp":1790500604150,"segment":2,"confidence":2.6029135483076136,"asi":{"hypothesis":"Levels written at or below the reader's per-device threshold were invisible; flooring every emission at 2*thr[d] (the pool's half_p50 median on-draw) can only turn already-detected events visible and is a no-op for mark-anchored gates.","confirmed":"primary +0.017795, p10 +0.011339 (up), fridge median +0.037990, wm median +0.013711, kettle/mw/dw bit-identical; checks pass.","measured_screen":"house_6 fridge F1 0.197->0.226 (2001->2191 preds); house_10 0.041->0.042 (1936->2541); house_17 and house_11 fridge unchanged.","refuted_this_iteration":"The protocol-anchored fridge duty-cell re-anchor guard is dead code: it never fired on any of the 20 pool houses (0 prints in runs/86.log) because the candidate anchor band holds fewer than DUTY_CELL_MIN=300 pre-span events; the 154 W '2*thr' reading was the median of all extracted events, not the fridge draw.","new_diagnosis":"On refit houses the GT fridge cycles are 0.3-1.0 min pulses every ~45-50 min; the mined most-regular 20-100 W / 11-37 min cell is a competing periodic load and only 2/12-4/12 of emitted runs start at a real pulse. Fridge cell identity needs a physical criterion, not interval regularity alone.","next_action_hint":"Attack fridge cell selection: prefer isolated, amplitude-stable, fridge-duty-fraction cells over the minimum interval-CV cell; then resume the B3 self-training bet.","carried_metrics_note":"b1_*, b2_* and transfer_mean_f1 are carried from the last measured values in .auto/log.jsonl, not re-measured this run."}}
+{"run":87,"commit":"2f0ee0f","metric":0.354623,"metrics":{"mean_device_f1_p10":0.33669,"transfer_mean_f1":0.151921,"median_kettle_f1":0.55514,"median_microwave_f1":0.266004,"median_fridge_f1":0.370963,"median_washing_machine_f1":0.242345,"median_dishwasher_f1":0.346705,"b1_events_mined":5260,"b1_enroll_top1_enc":0.84,"b1_enroll_top1_raw":0.65,"b1_cross_house_top1":0.21,"b1_gate_kettle_kept_frac":0.813,"b1_gate_mw_kept_frac":0.853,"b2_probe_mw_iso_mean":0.34,"b2_probe_iso_all_mean":0.61,"device_balanced_mean":0.358294,"house_1_v4_mean":0.539774,"v4_n_pairs":66,"v4_n_houses":20,"fridge_median_delta":0,"primary_delta":0},"status":"discard","description":"Iteration goal: repair the fridge duty-band selection that m20 diagnosed as the remaining structural prize (refit/house_10 fridge 0.041, house_17 fridge 0.042).\n\nMEASURED RESULT: pool primary 0.354623 (p10 0.336690, device_balanced 0.358294, house_1 0.539774, 66 pairs / 20 houses, all 5 seeds), identical to the floor 2f0ee0f to six decimals, with the dead m19 fridge re-anchor guard deleted from model.py. 109s, checksPass true. The guard printed 0 times across all 20 houses, so its deletion is inert pool-wide - verified both by a bit-identical 4-house subset A/B and by this full run.\n\nThree repairs were implemented, screened on the subset refit/house_10,refit/house_17,refit/house_6,ukdale/house_1 (--seeds 2026 --workers 1, sequential logs give house attribution), then reverted:\n1. Mark-derived mining duration window: subset mean 0.364151 -> 0.350107, fridge median 0.257162 -> 0.193965. REFUTED.\n2. Reader-anchored amp band on the mark branch of the fridge gate: inert, because that branch is the elif of `if fridge_band is not None` and never runs where a band was mined. REFUTED.\n3. Reader-anchored union (2*thr +- REL_AMP inside the home's mark duration window) on the live band branch: added 734/23/1118/291 preds on the four houses, yet subset mean -> 0.363897 and fridge median -> 0.256019. REFUTED.\n\nMECHANISM DISCOVERY (the durable finding): evaluation.score_episodes matches onsets within tau and then discards a matched pair whose len_pred/len_gt falls outside DURATION_BAND. The fridge run-basis emits 20-30min runs (band dur 10-37min) while refit reader cycles measure 0.3-1.0min (union-mask walk, consistent with 1956/2436 GT cycle counts), so those onsets cannot score even when they coincide. Refit hosts two coexisting ~66min-period loads: the model's ~1900 long runs and the reader's brief pulse at each cycle start. The graded pulse has no extractable aggregate signature - not the mined band population, not the 2*thr population - so both the band and the reader level fail, and shortening the mining window made it worse. The refit fridge prizes (house_10 +0.0044, house_17 +0.0044) are unreachable by band edits; the reachable fridge work is house_6 (0.226 -> 0.33) where emitted onsets partly coincide with reader pulses.\n\nCarried counters unchanged (b1/b2 tracks not exercised). Durable lessons written to .auto/ideas.md as m21 with explicit DO-NOT-RETRY markers for all three repairs.","title":"Refuted fridge band repairs; m19 guard proven inert (pool flat)","summary":"Three fridge band repairs refuted on a 4-house screen; pool primary unchanged at 0.354623 and the deleted m19 guard changed nothing.","timestamp":1790501204950,"segment":2,"confidence":2.300858935790804,"asi":{"hypothesis":"The fridge duty band's duration window (10-37min) is the last calibration-derived quantity silently disabling fridge detection on refit, so re-deriving it from the home's own mark or admitting the reader-anchored 2*thr population would restore the graded cycles.","rollback_reason":"All three variants were refuted by subset measurements (fridge median -0.063, inert branch, -0.0011) and the cleanup state reproduced the floor exactly, giving zero primary delta against the +0.01 keep bar.","next_action_hint":"Do not retry the three listed fridge band repairs; the refit fridge graded cycles are extraction-limited. Move to B3 (self-training over the unlabeled year) per the big-bet order, and if the fridge is revisited, target house_6 where onsets partly align.","refuted_repairs":["mark-derived mining duration window","reader-anchored band on the mark elif branch","reader-anchored union on the live band branch"],"subset_screen":"refit/house_10,refit/house_17,refit/house_6,ukdale/house_1 seeds 2026 workers 1","measured_primary_delta":0}}
