d apply the run-87-refuted reader-draw band.\n\nMEASURED RESULT (subset refit/house_10, refit/house_17, refit/house_6, ukdale/house_1, seeds 2026, workers 1): the path fires on 3 of 4 houses but every winner is a sparse day-scale cell - house_10 R=0.418 n=20 T=8264min, house_17 R=0.342 n=36 T=1769min, ukdale/house_1 R=0.364 n=34 T=4401min - while the box populations are Poisson-like (R_pop 0.006-0.017, cv_pop 0.92-3.31). Subset mean 0.364151 -> 0.347702, fridge median 0.257162 -> 0.183141. REFUTED and reverted.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE RUN after `git checkout -- src/experiments/04_autoresearch/model.py` (src diff empty, byte-identical to the floor): primary 0.354623, p10 0.336690, device_balanced 0.358294, house_1 0.539774, medians kettle 0.555140 / mw 0.266004 / fridge 0.370963 / wm 0.242345 / dw 0.346705, 66 pairs / 20 houses, 81 s, checksPass true. Identical to the floor, so the run is a discard.\n\nSTRUCTURAL CONCLUSION (third independent demonstration): narrowing the fridge's duration hypothesis space always loses - the wide m16 fallback band is a measured local optimum, the run-87 mark-derived window lost -0.063 fridge median, and the day-scale Rayleigh cells lost -0.074. The graded refit fridge cycles are 0.3-1.0min while DUTY_DUR_S = 600-2400s excludes them, and the 10-40min compressor-class box population is a near-Poisson mixture, not a duty device. Durable lessons in .auto/ideas.md m22, including the note to delete the m19 reader-draw guard before ever making the cell path reachable.","title":"Fridge cell gate dead pool-wide; Rayleigh repair refuted (flat)","summary":"Census: the fridge duty-cell path fires on 0 blocks. Making it reachable via Rayleigh folding fires but picks day-scale cells; fridge median -0.074.","timestamp":1790501574753,"segment":2,"confidence":2.0616187734790437,"asi":{"hypothesis":"The fridge duty-cell path is dead pool-wide because of a combinatorially impossible count gate plus an interval-CV criterion that cannot survive the extractor's ~1/3 subsampling; a Rayleigh phase-folding criterion with the home's own population as the regularity floor would give a selective, regular fridge band.","rollback_reason":"Reachable path selected sparse day-scale cells (T 29h to 5.7d, n 20-36) and lost 0.074 fridge median on the subset; reverted byte-exactly and the pool re-measured flat at 0.354623.","next_action_hint":"Stop editing the fridge band - the wide m16 fallback is a measured local optimum, confirmed three times. Delete the m19 reader-draw guard before any future attempt to make the cell path reachable. Start B3 (self-training) on a device whose weak median is not band-limited.","refuted_repairs":["count-gate-only repair (inert: interval CV is the second dead gate)","Rayleigh phase-folding cell selection with the home's own population floor"],"census_findings":{"fridge_cell_path_fired":0,"fridge_fallback_blocks":63,"named_dw_chains_all_blocks":0,"kettle_sustained_windows":"87/180"},"subset_screen":"refit/house_10,refit/house_17,refit/house_6,ukdale/house_1 seeds 2026 workers 1"}}
