+{"run":90,"commit":"2f0ee0f","metric":0.352638,"metrics":{"mean_device_f1_p10":0.346326,"transfer_mean_f1":0.151921,"median_kettle_f1":0.55514,"median_microwave_f1":0.267281,"median_fridge_f1":0.370963,"median_washing_machine_f1":0.242345,"median_dishwasher_f1":0.388346,"b1_events_mined":5260,"b1_enroll_top1_enc":0.84,"b1_enroll_top1_raw":0.65,"b1_cross_house_top1":0.21,"b1_gate_kettle_kept_frac":0.813,"b1_gate_mw_kept_frac":0.853,"b2_probe_mw_iso_mean":0.34,"b2_probe_iso_all_mean":0.61,"device_balanced_mean":0.359112,"house_1_v4_mean":0.540104,"v4_n_pairs":66,"v4_n_houses":20,"fridge_median_delta":0,"primary_delta":-0.0019850000000000145},"status":"discard","description":"Goal (from m23): the per-pair dump showed two dishwashers dead on EVERY seed - refit/house_10 (0 of 86 GT cycles, all 5 seeds) and refit/house_13 (~1 of 73) - worth about +0.012 primary if both reached F1 0.4. Both were diagnosed as the SAME root cause: bands derived from a mark whose own run is structureless.\n\n(1) MERGE GAP. refit/house_10's profile printed heater_gap_merge=70min, and 70 min is exactly the `4200.0 / DW30_GRID_S` fallback, reached only when max_gap == 0, i.e. when the marks show no internal pause at all. Its hs lower margin of 0.75 means every mark run is fully ON (one block per window), so no gap is ever measured. In the eval window that evidence-free 70-min gap fuses distinct cycles into one long run, and the span band (8-21 min, from the marks' own runs) then rejects every one. With no pause evidence the honest gap is one grid step; a single-block mark also means a genuine cycle's heater is continuous, so nothing needs bridging. Applied to both mirrored profiles (_dw30_profile and _wm30_profile).\n\n(2) DUTY FLOOR. A mark run IS the merged region above the heater threshold, so hs = 1.0 minus whatever dips the merge bridged. When every mark run is fully ON the floor of 0.75*min(hss) = 0.75 carries no information and excludes genuinely partial-duty cycles: other houses' dw mar